{
  "requirement": "For node reads, the SDK constructs a `Snapshot` from\nthe contents returned by `Domain::node_content` and their\n`NodeContents::fingerprint` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.fingerprint`, without another read.\n\n```rust,ignore\n#[non_exhaustive]\npub struct Snapshot<T> {\n    pub content: T,\n    pub fingerprint: Fingerprint,\n}\n\nimpl<T> Snapshot<T> {\n    pub fn new(content: T, fingerprint: Fingerprint) -> Self;\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl<T: Clone> Clone for Snapshot<T>;\nimpl<T: Debug> Debug for Snapshot<T>;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.graph.snapshot`.\n\n**Obligations and the tests that cover them**\n\n- **Construction from `Domain::node_content` and `NodeContents::fingerprint`.**\n  - `direct_reads_return_complete_unicode_contents_and_snapshots` (`crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs`) reads a snapshot for empty and large Unicode contents. It asserts that `snapshot.content.format()` and `snapshot.fingerprint` equal the original contents and `fp(original)`. It also asserts that the recorded dependency carries that same fingerprint.\n  - `snapshots_record_exact_reads_and_retain_distinct_versions` checks `read_snapshot` against the \"before\" fingerprint. It then changes the contents and confirms that a later read yields \"after\" while the earlier snapshot is unchanged.\n  - `identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot` (`crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs`) asserts `snapshot.content.fingerprint() == snapshot.fingerprint` and `snapshot.fingerprint.value == \"before\"`.\n  - `requirement_edges_and_input_freshness_use_the_sdk` (`src/sdk.rs`) compares fingerprints against the real Habeas domain.\n  - `graph_tools_record_delivered_snapshots_and_prepared_pages_do_not_record_delivery` (`crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs`) asserts that the dependency from an agent `read_node` carries the snapshot fingerprint.\n  - `explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots` asserts the same through the `ask` path.\n- **No other read.**\n  - `snapshots_record_exact_reads_and_retain_distinct_versions` asserts the exact read log `[1, 1, 1, 2]`.\n  - `direct_reads_return_complete_unicode_contents_and_snapshots` asserts `[1, 1]`.\n  - `identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot` asserts `[1]`. The domain contents change after the read, yet the snapshot's fingerprint and `format()` output stay at \"before\".\n- **`Snapshot::new` and the public `content` and `fingerprint` fields.** `callers_can_pair_content_with_its_fingerprint` (`crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs`) builds a snapshot through `new` and asserts both fields.\n- **`Clone` and `Debug` implementations.** I found no test that exercises these. They are plain `#[derive(Clone, Debug)]` on `Snapshot` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph.rs`. A derive has no conditional and no transformation of its own, so I treat the untested derives as exempt.\n- **`#[non_exhaustive]`.** This is a compile-time attribute on the type. It is present in the source, and the attribute needs no behavioral test.\n\nThe cited `requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.fingerprint` is context only. The tests apply it by comparing the snapshot fingerprint with the contents' own `fingerprint()`.\n\nI found no unmarked relevant tests and no unacknowledged gaps.",
